 "evidence": "A calculation on the design routing's own floor, works and climate with a lake rule that fills each hollow as one water: the factor on the open water's evaporation, the weirs' shares and the near-side sea's levels are set again by the procedures that set them on the present rule, the search for a part's level taking the cells that join at one level together. It is a steady state: a lake stands wherever its supply would keep it, however long it would take to fill. The climate is the design climate, run on a surface with the design's seas and lakes; no climate has been run on the state found here. Nothing is validated against an observation.",
 "reading_rule": "Levels in m above the redrawn common level, flows in m3/s, areas in km2, volumes in km3. factor: closing gives final_drainage.budget's figures with every sea at the common level, on the corrected rule at factor 1 and at the factor that step gives, and on the present rule at the design's factor; surplus_m3s at a rule's own factor is what its budget still leaves over. seas: each water of the design routing (the near-side sea as its two parts) in the design and rebalanced; loses is the open water's loss beyond the rain on it at the state's own factor, receives what rivers, overflows and works bring it. governed is the state the weirs are set on, the near-side sea at the common level: released is what each weir or branch lets go and arrived what reaches its sea beyond its own rivers; branch_flows_m3s is each branch's flow at each of its put-ins and take-outs in order. near_side.history is each routing of the parted sea with the balance each part was left with; control is the neck read from its record on the design's rivers beside the design's steady state. near_side.sills_met lists each sill of a basin beside a part at which the part's level came to rest with water left over: the sill, what was left over, the basin's ground below the sill, what the basin loses to the air, its lowest point, and what was done (the part tried with the basin under its water, or left at the sill spilling into the basin). near_side.to_spare_at_the_design_levels_m3s is what the rivers that reach both parts bring beyond what the parts would lose at their design levels on the new factor. lakes are off the seas; shore_cells_not_held and ground_below_and_joined_km2 are lake_support.py's measures; lakes.closer lists the largest lakes as bodies (a hollow's one water) and the largest that pass nothing on, each with its place on today's Moon and in the settled frame. changed sets the rebalanced lakes and seas against the design's cell by cell. land_and_lakes_send_the_seas_m3s is what reaches the seas less what the works and overflows carry from sea to sea. waterways gives each named waterway's flow where it ends, at its design mouth cell, and at its design head cell; where its sea has risen up its design course, the rebalanced flow is read at the last cell of that course not under the sea, the design's flow at that cell is given beside it, and change sets the one against the other. For a waterway that loses more than a twentieth of its flow, the largest lakes its design course crosses are listed.",
